<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_66b005a6484e5a6e96e40015102d69efc8bc0d0cc9a2a807f86d748d49b3068d_n0046/e_0007> <http://digistrucmed.org/hasNormalization> <http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_66b005a6484e5a6e96e40015102d69efc8bc0d0cc9a2a807f86d748d49b3068d_n0046/e_0007/normalization> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/semantic-unit/lu_66b005a6484e5a6e96e40015102d69efc8bc0d0cc9a2a807f86d748d49b3068d_n0046> <http://digistrucmed.org/titleOrContext> "e high value of beta-blocker therapy among HF patients. A model-based analysis, using generic beta-blocker costs, found beta-blocker therapy was high value.<sup>4</sup> These results were consistent with earlier model-based cost-effectiveness analyses<sup>5-7</sup> and a trial-based economic analysis of the US Carvedilol Heart Failure (CHF) Trials Program.<sup>8</sup> Each of these studies also found treatment with a beta blocker was high value despite using previously higher beta-blocker costs." .
